{
  "_comment": [
    "Tools agentconf knows EXIST. This is not the adapter registry and must never be confused",
    "with it. An entry here means 'we know this tool and where to look'; an adapter in",
    "adapters/ means 'a canary proved this tool reads this file'.",
    "",
    "Keeping those separate is the whole design. Every `candidates` path below is a HYPOTHESIS",
    "— usually from vendor docs, sometimes from what another tool writes — and a hypothesis is",
    "exactly what `agentconf scan` reports as unmanaged rather than silently wiring up.",
    "",
    "confidence: documented | reported | unverified",
    "  documented  the vendor's own docs name this path",
    "  reported    a third party (e.g. rulesync's target list) writes here; the vendor has not confirmed it",
    "  unverified  a guess from the directory layout"
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "id": "claude",
      "name": "Claude Code",
      "bins": [
        "claude"
      ],
      "configDirs": [
        "~/.claude"
      ],
      "candidates": [
        {
          "path": "~/.claude/CLAUDE.md",
          "kind": "instructions",
          "confidence": "documented"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory",
      "adapter": "claude-instructions"
    },
    {
      "id": "codex",
      "name": "OpenAI Codex CLI",
      "bins": [
        "codex"
      ],
      "configDirs": [
        "~/.codex"
      ],
      "candidates": [
        {
          "path": "~/.codex/AGENTS.md",
          "kind": "instructions",
          "confidence": "documented"
        },
        {
          "path": "~/.codex/rules/*.rules",
          "kind": "policy",
          "confidence": "documented"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-configuration/agents-md",
      "adapter": "codex-instructions"
    },
    {
      "id": "droid",
      "name": "Factory droid",
      "bins": [
        "droid"
      ],
      "configDirs": [
        "~/.factory"
      ],
      "candidates": [
        {
          "path": "~/.factory/AGENTS.md",
          "kind": "instructions",
          "confidence": "reported"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The binary references CLAUDE.md as well as AGENTS.md. Which wins is unestablished — check before wiring, or an adapter may change behaviour rather than add it.",
      "docs": "https://docs.factory.ai/"
    },
    {
      "id": "gemini",
      "name": "Gemini CLI",
      "bins": [
        "gemini"
      ],
      "configDirs": [
        "~/.gemini"
      ],
      "candidates": [
        {
          "path": "~/.gemini/GEMINI.md",
          "kind": "instructions",
          "confidence": "documented"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli"
    },
    {
      "id": "goose",
      "name": "Block goose",
      "bins": [
        "goose"
      ],
      "configDirs": [
        "~/.config/goose"
      ],
      "candidates": [
        {
          "path": "~/.config/goose/.goosehints",
          "kind": "instructions",
          "confidence": "reported"
        }
      ],
      "note": "rulesync writes this path. `strings $(command -v goose)` showed ZERO references to '.goosehints' or 'AGENTS.md' on a machine where goose is installed — unproven, not disproven, since a stripped or compressed binary can hide a string. Do not wire without a canary.",
      "docs": "https://block.github.io/goose/"
    },
    {
      "id": "copilot",
      "name": "GitHub Copilot CLI",
      "bins": [
        "copilot"
      ],
      "configDirs": [
        "~/.copilot",
        "~/.config/github-copilot"
      ],
      "candidates": [
        {
          "path": "~/.copilot/copilot-instructions.md",
          "kind": "instructions",
          "confidence": "reported"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "https://docs.github.com/en/copilot"
    },
    {
      "id": "cursor",
      "name": "Cursor",
      "bins": [
        "cursor",
        "cursor-agent"
      ],
      "configDirs": [
        "~/.cursor"
      ],
      "candidates": [
        {
          "path": "~/.cursor/rules",
          "kind": "instructions",
          "confidence": "unverified"
        }
      ],
      "note": "An editor rather than a CLI agent. A canary needs cursor-agent, not the GUI.",
      "docs": "https://docs.cursor.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": "windsurf",
